   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "By 1989, prices were rising so fast that money lost its value from week to week. The OECD put the rise in prices during that year at about two thousand seven hundred per cent.",
     "tag": "estimate",
     "cite": "§3"
    },
    {
     "text": "In March 1989, Ante Marković became the federal prime minister.",
     "tag": "established",
     "cite": "§3"
    },
    {
     "text": "On the first of January 1990, Marković's government introduced a new dinar, worth ten thousand old ones, and pegged it to the German mark.",
     "tag": "record",
     "cite": "§3"
    },
    {
     "text": "The World Bank reported that monthly inflation fell close to zero between April and June.",
     "tag": "estimate",
     "cite": "§3"
    },
    {
     "text": "But his reforms lost support during 1990.",
     "tag": "established",
     "cite": "§3"
    }
   ],
